{"uncertainty": 0.35, "outcome": "Self-checking coverage testbench irq_ctrl_cov_tb.sv is submitted. It extends the approved idle testbench, and its coverage report lists every point that cannot be reached and why. No coverage numbers are claimed. The figures will come from the platform's coverage.read run over this testbench and the approved irq_ctrl.v.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "coverage_report", "title": "irq_ctrl coverage closure report (pre-run; figures pending the platform coverage.read run)", "summary": "Scope: the approved design [artifact:prj-63d6b8e26c.design-under-test.a1], reviewed under [evidence:prj-63d6b8e26c.design-under-test.e1], for [requirement:req-1e26d9c190].\n\nStarting point: the approved idle testbench [artifact:prj-63d6b8e26c.testbench.a1] passes 5 checks ([evidence:prj-63d6b8e26c.testbench.e1], [run:run-0001]). It only resets the block and reads back ENABLE and MODE, so it never raises a source, sets pending, raises irq or acknowledges anything.\n\nNew testbench (irq_ctrl_cov_tb.sv) drives one bus into two instances, irq_ctrl #(N=8) and irq_ctrl #(N=32). The N=32 instance is a configuration irq_ctrl.v supports (N 2 to 32); it reaches bits that are constant at N=8. The testbench file also holds a cycle-level reference model, irq_ctrl_cov_model. After every clock edge, and at each of the four addresses, both DUT instances are compared against their model instance. Directed absolute checks are added at chosen points.\n\nStimulus, intended to reach every line and branch of irq_ctrl.v:\n1. Reset values.\n2. ENABLE and MODE written with all ones, all zeros, A5/5A and 3C/C3 patterns, so every wdata, enable and mode bit moves both ways.\n3. Level detection with every source masked, so pending is set while irq stays low.\n4. W1C clears in three slices.\n5. A priority walk with all sources pending and enabled, acknowledging ids 0 to 31 in order. irq_id runs 0..7 at N=8 and 0..31 at N=32. Ids 8 to 31 take the ack_hit-false path at N=8.\n6. Detection winning over a same-edge W1C and over a CLAIM acknowledge.\n7. Rising-edge mode with a held source, where a clear sticks and a falling edge detects nothing.\n8. Mixed modes with an enable mask, including pending-but-disabled sources.\n9. A reset asserted mid-operation with non-zero registers, then released.\n\nPoints expected to stay uncovered, each justified (no exclusion pragmas are used anywhere):\n(a) unused_wdata = &{1'b0, wdata} is constant 0 by construction, in both instances. It is unreachable: a lint sink, not functional logic.\n(b) At N=8, rdata[30:8] is always 0, because the register case writes only rdata[N-1:0], or rdata[31] and rdata[4:0]. It is unreachable at this parameter.\n(c) At N=8, irq_id[4:3] is always 0 because the highest source id is 7. It is unreachable at this parameter.\n(b) and (c) are exercised in the N=32 instance's separate points.\n\nThe pass/fail verdict, line/toggle/branch percentages and per-point hits are not known here. They are for the platform's coverage.read run to report against the requirement's bounds."}], "files": [{"path": "irq_ctrl_cov_tb.sv", "kind": "testbench", "title": "irq_ctrl_cov_tb.sv: self-checking coverage testbench for irq_ctrl.v (N=8 and N=32) with a reference model", "summary": "Extends the approved idle testbench [artifact:prj-63d6b8e26c.testbench.a1] to drive the approved RTL [artifact:prj-63d6b8e26c.design-under-test.a1] for [requirement:req-1e26d9c190].\n\nIt checks two instances, irq_ctrl #(8) and irq_ctrl #(32), against an in-file reference model on every cycle and every address, plus directed checks. It covers sources, level and edge detection, W1C, CLAIM acknowledge, priority, masking and mid-run reset.\n\nIt prints the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line with the run nonce. It uses no $fopen, $system, $c, DPI, `include, Verilator configuration or coverage pragmas.", "entry": "irq_ctrl_cov_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["Every line and every if/case branch of irq_ctrl.v is expected to be reached by this stimulus. This is not yet shown by any run.", "The only toggle points expected to stay at zero are: unused_wdata in both instances, and rdata[30:8] and irq_id[4:3] in the N=8 instance. This is not yet shown by any run.", "The reference model is expected to agree with irq_ctrl.v on every compared cycle. A model or expectation error would surface as a failed check in the platform run.", "Whether line, toggle and branch reach the requirement's bounds is unknown here; the bounds were not given to this seat."], "escalation": null, "notes": "I did not run any tool, and I report no coverage figures. [run:run-0001] is the earlier idle-testbench simulation, cited only as the baseline; it is not a run of this testbench.\n\nDesign choice for review: the N=32 instance adds coverage points of its own. It is driven and checked as fully as N=8, so it raises the reachable toggle ceiling instead of hiding gaps. If reviewers want coverage measured at N=8 only, delete the dut32/ref32 instances and the 32-bit expectations. The N=8 toggle ceiling then drops, because of the 26 constant bits listed in the report.\n\nBuild risk: Verilator might warn on the N=32 ack_hit comparison, which is always true when wdata[4:0] < 32. If the gate treats that warning as fatal, the build fails and the N=32 instance must be dropped.\n\nDetection-wins and rising-edge behaviour follow the RTL header comments, not a separate specification, since interface_spec.md was not provided to this seat."}
